t the `provider` variable, which could lead to issues if the `InstanceType` constructor relies on it being non-null.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/profiling/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/profiling/InstanceType.java-DST-ADDITION-1202-1258-VariableDeclarationStatement","path":"x-pack/plugin/profiling/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/profiling/InstanceType.java","srcDst":"DST","content":"String provider \u003d (String) source.get(\"cloud.provider\");","nodeType":"ADDITION","treeType":"VariableDeclarationStatement","descendantSimpleNames":["String","provider","String","source","get"],"identifiers":["provider"],"startLine":38,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":38,"endLineOffset":64,"length":57,"subs":[]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/profiling/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/profiling/InstanceType.java-DST-ADDITION-1661-1731-IfStatement","path":"x-pack/plugin/profiling/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/profiling/InstanceType.java","srcDst":"DST","content":"if (instanceType !\u003d null) {\n            return instanceType;\n        }","nodeType":"ADDITION","treeType":"IfStatement","descendantSimpleNames":["instanceType","instanceType"],"startLine":47,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":49,"endLineOffset":9,"length":71,"subs":[]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/profiling/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/profiling/InstanceType.java-SRC-SRC_UPDATE-2861-2869-SimpleName","path":"x-pack/plugin/profiling/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/profiling/InstanceType.java","srcDst":"SRC","content":"provider","nodeType":"SRC_UPDATE","treeType":"SimpleName","descendantSimpleNames":["provider"],"startLine":77,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":77,"endLineOffset":23,"length":9,"subs":[]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/profiling/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/profiling/InstanceType.java-DST-DST_UPDATE-1977-1983-SimpleName","path":"x-pack/plugin/profiling/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/profiling/InstanceType.java","srcDst":"DST","content":"region","nodeType":"DST_UPDATE","treeType":"SimpleName","descendantSimpleNames":["region"],"startLine":58,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":58,"endLineOffset":21,"length":7,"subs":[]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/profiling/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/profiling/InstanceType.java-DST-SEMANTIC_CONTEXT-1970-1991-VariableDeclarationStatement","path":"x-pack/plugin/profiling/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/profiling/InstanceType.java","srcDst":"DST","content":"String region \u003d null;","nodeType":"SEMANTIC_CONTEXT","treeType":"VariableDeclarationStatement","descendantSimpleNames":["String","region"],"startLine":58,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":58,"endLineOffset":29,"length":22}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":51,"line":51,"comment_lines":["[][51]"],"review_comment":["I missed this in the last review but it is actually not required that we bump the index template version on every change. Instead, it is sufficient to bump it once per release because no cluster can observe the intermediate index template versions.\r\n\r\nLong story short: Can you please change this value to `5` (which applies to 8.14.0) and merge the comments accordingly to include all changes that went into version `5`?","That is a good point I already thought of. My conclusion was that I do not know whether version 5 or 6 has already been deployed (locally) and used by developers. And if you don\u0027t know that, why risking to break things even if it is just one or two people?\r\n\r\nWhat is the downside of increasing the version several times per release cycle?","As discussed offline, it\u0027s less risky to bump the version all the time, even if this means version jumps between releases (which are harmless) so let\u0027s stick to this convention in the future."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/profiling/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/profiling/ProfilingIndexTemplateRegistry.java","id":35439,"created_at":"2024-03-22T12:32:01Z","original_position":6,"side":"RIGHT","position":6,"submitted_on_commit":"d95e7c76a3bc78362fd9a3715b9b0ba581719027","diff_hunk":"@@ -47,13 +47,14 @@ public class ProfilingIndexTemplateRegistry extends IndexTemplateRegistry {\n     // version 4: Added \u0027service.name\u0027 keyword mapping to profiling-events\n     // version 5: Add optional component template \u0027\u003cidx-name\u003e@custom\u0027 to all index templates that reference component templates\n     // version 6: Added \u0027host.arch\u0027 keyword mapping to profiling-hosts\n-    public static final int INDEX_TEMPLATE_VERSION \u003d 6;\n+    // version 7: Added \u0027host.type\u0027, \u0027cloud.provider\u0027, \u0027cloud.region\u0027 keyword mappings to profiling-hosts\n+    public static final int INDEX_TEMPLATE_VERSION \u003d 7;","submitted_line":51},"generatedCommentsNodes":[]}],"coveredGroundTruth":0,"uncoveredGroundTruth":1,"coveredHunkNodes":4,"uncoveredHunkNodes":24,"timing":28794,"tokensIn":8173,"tokensOut":585}